Terminal 209 -> 211, and every raster receipt in the corpus overstates its coverage\n\nVF54 read four families I had described as needing only an independent\nread. Two are now proven: md_10105_early-set and rcap-hi-custom-pleading,\nfifteen of fifteen each. Two fail on obligations no lane had measured.\n\nIT CHECKED MY PREMISE AND HALF OF IT WAS WRONG. I said each already\ncarried a bound RASTER_PASS. The receipts in RASTER_QUEUE.json do bind\nthe bytes on disk; the ones in raster-runs/admitted/ do not, for two of\nthe four, because FIX141 and FIX142 rewrote those canonicals after those\nruns. Both files say RASTER_PASS. A reader who opens admitted/ and stops\nis reading a pass over superseded bytes.\n\nTHE LARGER ONE, WHICH I MEASURED ACROSS ALL 220 RECEIPTS RATHER THAN\nTAKING IT: every one says coversTheWholeFamily true, and 216 name a\ndelivered fixture the gate did not render. 172 cover canonical.pdf alone.\nThe receipt is not lying -- it defines its terms, and whatCompleteMeansHere\nsays in its own words that boundary and route fixtures are bound by hash\nbut not rendered. What is wrong is the name. A boundary fixture is what a\nparticipant receives on the boundary route, and no human and no detector\nhas looked at a rendered page of one. Hawaii is the sharpest case: twelve\nfixtures, one rendered, its own report carrying routeArtifactRasterPending\ntrue beside a flag saying the family is whole.\n\nThat is the same asymmetry the NE/WV R2 review found in one proposal on\nthree families -- measure both, compare one -- sitting in the central\ngate on 216. It is a definitional question about what the visual gate is\nfor and it is not mine to settle, so it is recorded for Roger rather than\nacted on: it decides whether 194 proven families are proven on the packet\nor on half of it. Nothing is withdrawn; every canonical was rendered and\nevery fixture is hash-bound.\n\nVF54's own findings are participant-facing. Missouri names three\ngovernment agencies as Defendants on a form the participant signs under\npenalty of perjury, and neither guidance file contains the word serve,\nservice or notice in any sense -- the only matches are inside an agency's\nname. The record answers it unambiguously and the packet withheld the\nanswer. Michigan writes a live case number into an UNNAMED source widget\non delivered pages 2 and 3 -- no /T, so it appears in no map row, no\ncaption evidence and no counter -- and the glyph counter reads zero\nbecause it measures against all 104 flattened appearances rather than the\n8 declared writes. The write is correct and must stay; it is undeclared,\nso a participant told to check what the platform filled in is pointed at\none case number and given three.\n\nTwo Maryland reads I would have got wrong without its work: the packet\nships the General Waiver twice and COMPONENT_SET still passes, because\nthe guide says in terms not to sign both; and 517 px of added ink in a\nselection control is the COURT'S OWN writing rule reappearing when the\npacket drops an opaque dropdown, not platform ink.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W3FAJNotS5DdvyJS1khjid","timestamp":"2026-09-10T17:06:51Z","author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"}},"repository":{"id":1248656766,"node_id":"R_kgDOSmz9fg","name":"legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","full_name":"Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","private":false,"owner":{"login":"Roger-LegalEase","id":287531360,"node_id":"U_kgDOESNhYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287531360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase","html_url":"https://github.com/Roger-LegalEase","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/